But there's a real connection you're circling, and it's more interesting than the one you named.

The payments layer already exists, and it's crowded. Six distinct protocols now handle agent-initiated payments — Mastercard Agent Pay, Visa Intelligent Commerce, Stripe ACP, Coinbase x402, Google AP2/UCP, and ATXP — and they aren't interoperable. An agent built for Stripe ACP can't natively transact on Mastercard Agent Pay. x402 got a Linux Foundation launch in July. This is a solved-ish, extremely well-funded problem. You're not adding to it in a weekend, and you shouldn't try, because money plus agents plus a rushed build is how you end up in a thread you don't want.
